From 283efe72006b7eaa9c31dd428853ddda5c1e2ca0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:21:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 73/79] soc: qcom: oplus-camres: unified vote architecture +
 protocol identical to v1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Complete rework of the ownership layer. The wire protocol (sns_send,
sns_parse_ack, AON subscribe, REVOKE, RELEASE) is byte-for-byte
identical to the original working driver (81243488c) — verified by
diff on every protocol function.

Ownership: a single consumers counter. Every path — misc ioctls,
runtime PM (device-link supplier resume/suspend), kernel API, probe
votes — funnels through camres_acquire_vote/camres_release_vote.
During CONFIGURING all acquires park on state_wq; DEINIT waits for
consumers==0 and forces the handback; INIT resolves the parked
waiters.

Runtime PM starts SUSPENDED (not set_active): pm_runtime_set_active()
created an RPM_ACTIVE zombie that the PM core's already-active
short-circuit skipped forever — the resume callback (and the park
logic inside it) never fired.  Device links use DL_FLAG_PM_RUNTIME
without AUTOREMOVE (a child unbind would permanently drop the PM
chain).  PM is enabled BEFORE i2c_add_adapter (the PM core silently
ignores suppliers with disabled runtime PM).

The manual sysfs vote is gone (duplicate of ioctl ACQUIRE, unauditable);
ap_hold is read-only.  A dedicated workqueue replaces the deprecated
system_wq.  Consumer drivers (smartsens-sc, dw9719) are completely
vanilla — no bus-management code in them.

(cherry picked from commit 4c743c779b1bc60ab334a8f2625090a08ad4869c)
